rl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt","html_url":"https://github.com/mcwitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-17T18:55:29Z","updated_at":"2026-08-17T18:55:29Z","body":"🤖 Closing update: the diagnosis here was premature. Further isolation shows the registration failures we observed were caused by the dynamic-slice fusion pass wrapping Mosaic-GPU collective custom calls and dropping their collective memory space; the escaped parameter then fails window registration from default memory. With `--xla_gpu_enable_dynamic_slice_fusion=false` (plus the `cuda_async` allocator), the same programs pass on stock nightlies at 4 and 8 ranks with no wheel changes.\n\nWith correct coloring, each executable's collective buffers coalesce into one `BufferAllocation` whose window registers at an aligned region base, so we could not reproduce an alignment failure independently. The unset `min_alignment` on the separate collective allocator entry ([se_gpu_pjrt_client.cc#L1579-L1592](https://github.com/openxla/xla/blob/60f8069e8b/xla/pjrt/gpu/se_gpu_pjrt_client.cc#L1579-L1592), cf. PR #44156) remains a latent gap only.\n\nWe plan to file the fusion/coloring issue separately with a self-contained repro.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"